# INV-09 — invented. Three overs a side; the extras that are easiest to score wrong.
# Edge cases: a no-ball and two byes (one run to the bowler, two byes to
# nobody, a ball faced); a no-ball and a leg bye (odd: ends change); a
# no-ball and four off the bat all run (the batter's four runs, no boundary);
# a no-ball hit for six; a wide and three run (four wides, odd: ends change);
# a striker run out going for a second bye (the bye stands, nobody's to the
# bowler); a run out off a wide after a run, at the bowler's end (two wides,
# no ball of the over: falls at 1.2); a bowled and a caught on free hits
# (neither stands); a wide that spoils nothing but the bowler's figures.
match INV-09
